A1. This one puts in his bill first and then goes to work. ~ MOSQUITO
A8. What a bear does in cold weather. (Phonetically speaking.) ~ REFERS
A14. An 'ouse electrically appointed. ~ OHM
A15. This one never makes a good mixer. ~ SNOB
A16. The muse of astronomy. ~ URANIA
A17. What a polite gentleman does when he makes a bow. ~ TIES
A19. In 1928 he made this on the stock-market. This year he made it at the stock yards. ~ KILLING
A21. This suggests a cumbersome thing. (It always keeps cool unless pickled.) ~ CU
A22. The kind of wood back of the silver screen. ~ HOLLY
A24. The finishing touch to a building. (plur.) ~ LIENS
A25. The leading lady in "Shenandoah." ~ SHE
A26. Tales of Baron Munchausen. ("Vas you there, Sharlie?") ~ LIES
A28. Measures adopted by both the "drys" and the "wets". (abbr.) ~ QTS
A29. A fortune-teller. ~ SEER
A30. A common stockholder. ~ SHED
A32. We are giving this burden to you although it should be on us. ~ ONUS
A34. This is sat on in rumble seats. ~ FLASK
A35. This one does not belong to the social set in kennel town. ~ CUR
A36. The shade of depression. ~ BLUE
A37. This has "floating power." ~ BOAT
A38. The leading man in "Herodias". ~ HE
A39. What seems to be brewing now. ~ MALT
A40. It has cause for crying out loud. ~ CROW
A41. A lie detector. ~ MA
A42. An old style conservative. ~ TORY
A43. There is a twist to this. ~ COIL
A44. France will need more than this to pay her debts. ~ SOU
A45. This will put you in a class by yourself. ~ ONION
A47. The kind of mayor Jimmy Walker was and is. ~ LATE
A48. What X marks. ~ SPOT
A49. To come down to earth. ~ LAND
A50. His speech on this received no applause. ~ AIR
A51. This one lives on nothing but hot-dogs. ~ FLEA
A53. A regular fellow. ~ GUY
A54. When you see the ocean tide you may know some ship has made many of these. ~ KNOTS
A56. Their thoughts were always inverse. ~ BARDS
A59. The end of the crisis and the beginning of the new issue. ~ IS
A60. The smallest members of the school. ~ MINNOWS
A62. They get some "jack" for this radio stuff. (Pearl and Benny) ~ SKIT
A63. A good thing to have for a second-hand car. ~ RESALE
A65. No prejudiced man can ever see this. ~ NAPE
A67. What a sailor calls a protection and a Scotchman calls a lie. ~ LEE
A68. This should have a voice in the affair. ~ LARYNX
A69. If you have solved this puzzle it may apply to you superlatively. ~ SMARTEST

D1. This one lives in a fur coat in the summer and a bathing suit in the winter. ~ MOTH
D2. There is a lot of this around Cincinnati. ~ OHIO
D3. A great detective. (As any woman nose.) ~ SMELLER
D4. This made her an usher. ~ US
D5. Say it with flowers and you'll never miss, But watch your step when you say it with this. ~ INK
D6. According to technocracy this has a price value. ~ TOIL
D7. Here is one of those crosswords that is neither vertical nor horizontal. ~ OBLIQUE
D8. The borrowed dinner gown that was sent in a suit case was returned in this. ~ RUINS
D9. Ocean fliers. ~ ERNS
D10. A camel without a hump. ~ FAG
D11. An edible tree. ~ EN
D12. Since the depression these have developed wings. ~ RICHES
D13. What! no spare-ribs? ~ SAUERKRAUT
D18. How Kelly made the base. ~ SLID
D20. In the past you would just take this for granted. ~ LETS
D23. A good way to start the year. ~ YE
D25. According to the latest mode this part of trousers will be satin. ~ SEAT
D27. What "Solomon in all his glory" was called by his wives. ~ SOLLY
D29. A raw deal. ~ SLAW
D30. An envious complexion. ~ SCHOOLGIRL
D31. Any color will do. ~ HUE
D33. This held the steering wheel. ~ NUT
D34. Shakespeare says the wise man knows himself to be this. ~ FOOL
D36. Bonded stockholders. ~ BARN
D37. This is a case for a lawyer. ~ BRIEF
D39. Caprice. ~ MOOD
D40. You may find this half cotton. ~ COT
D41. This sounds bossy. ~ MOO
D42. Minute. ~ TINY
D43. This old top is very popular in radio contests. (plur.) ~ CARTONS
D44. This gives us a bright idea. ~ SPARKLE
D46. A disturbance that may cause an uprising. ~ NAUSEA
D47. One animal in a million. ~ LION
D48. International affairs that are deep and never can be settled. ~ SEAS
D50. Shure and this is an added expanse at the hotel. ~ ANNEX
D52. Short weight. ~ LB
D54. A hot place for China. ~ KILN
D55. What he did to come across. ~ SWAM
D57. An engine often does this when someone chokes it. ~ DIES
D58. "Let it stand." (And it's not a subway rider.) ~ STET
D60. A month of sun days. ~ MAY
D61. A good place to go for relief. (That is if you wish to be relieved of bones.) ~ SPA
D64. Junior's old man. (abbr.) ~ SR
D66. If the word is hard this will make it harder. ~ ER


